{
  "title": "Drums Practice",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Read the chart, play",
        "the pads, watch your",
        "timing.",
        "",
        "Header: +3 s12 is",
        "3ms late, a spread",
        "of 12. Narrow is",
        "good.",
        "",
        "The bar at the",
        "bottom fills as the",
        "drill goes,",
        "hits/misses beside",
        "it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The list",
      "lines": [
        "Home: a circle each.",
        "JOG chooses, CLICK",
        "or its pad opens.",
        "Practice and Quiz",
        "are rings too: a",
        "circle per kind of",
        "drill, per quiz.",
        "",
        "Learning Path",
        "          the stages",
        "Practice  all drills",
        "Quiz      ear drills",
        "Progress  how far",
        "Settings  your setup",
        "",
        "PLAY on the Learning",
        "Path's map is",
        "Continue: the next",
        "step.",
        "",
        "CLICK opens, BACK",
        "goes up. MENU is",
        "help for the screen",
        "you are on,",
        "anywhere.",
        "",
        "A row shows your",
        "best clean speed:",
        "80%. A tick is",
        "learned, a ring",
        "played but not",
        "clean."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The sheet",
      "lines": [
        "SHIFT+CLICK on a row",
        "opens its options:",
        "",
        "I know this: skip",
        "I know it all: skip",
        "Undo skip",
        "Start the path here",
        "Test out: checkpoint",
        "Lessons",
        "Practise: Ladder",
        "Practise: Clock",
        "Settings...",
        "",
        "Only what fits the",
        "row is shown."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "PLAY   listen",
        "REC    practise,",
        "       scored",
        "The same button",
        "pauses; the other",
        "one switches.",
        "BACK   to the start,",
        "       then up",
        "",
        "A result: REC again,",
        "BACK to the start,",
        "CLICK the next",
        "drill. JOG back:",
        "look over the take",
        "as played. Only",
        "whole takes count.",
        "",
        "A groove: JOG on the",
        "ready screen picks",
        "its LEVEL, L0 to L4.",
        "The arrows: where it",
        "can still go."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Own pace (L0)",
      "lines": [
        "L0 is the whole",
        "groove, no clock.",
        "The bar stands",
        "still; arrows mark",
        "the next stack.",
        "",
        "Strike its drums,",
        "and only those,",
        "TOGETHER (60ms on",
        "normal) and the",
        "arrows move on.",
        "",
        "PLAY   hear the bar",
        "REC    begin, pause",
        "Learned: 90% right",
        "first time. The % is",
        "your pace, of the",
        "tempo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Knobs",
      "lines": [
        "In a drill:",
        "1  scrub, stopped",
        "8  speed, 50-120%",
        "",
        "Speed slows any",
        "drill, grooves and",
        "rudiments too. The",
        "tempo you play is",
        "what is recorded.",
        "",
        "In settings the",
        "knobs are the rows",
        "on screen, four to a",
        "page. Elsewhere they",
        "do nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The pads",
      "lines": [
        "Left half is your",
        "left hand, right",
        "half your right, in",
        "every layout.",
        "",
        "Settings > Pads:",
        "MPC      the default",
        "Family   by family",
        "Centre   kick, snare",
        "         centred",
        "GM       Move's own",
        "Mirror   two-handed",
        "Custom   your own",
        "Sticking snare only",
        "Flip mirrors it.",
        "",
        "Pad map: every pad",
        "named. CLICK on a",
        "preset copies it to",
        "Custom; PAD picks,",
        "JOG sounds, KNOB 1",
        "both halves, BACK",
        "saves.",
        "",
        "New to them?",
        "Learning Path >",
        "0 Hello, kit > Ear >",
        "Meet the pads shows",
        "each one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Colours",
      "lines": [
        "green   you got it",
        "amber   right drum,",
        "        WRONG HAND",
        "azure   right drum,",
        "        wrong volume",
        "red     you missed",
        "yellow  your finger",
        "violet  now",
        "purple  coming up",
        "pulse   Study waits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Study",
      "lines": [
        "Settings > Advanced",
        "> Practice > Study",
        "stops the",
        "scroll ON a note you",
        "missed. The lane",
        "names it; Guide pads",
        "pulse it.",
        "",
        "One press carries",
        "on."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Scoring",
      "lines": [
        "Four things, counted",
        "apart, because each",
        "is fixed",
        "differently:",
        "",
        "timing   mean+spread",
        "drum     hit or miss",
        "hand     sticking",
        "dynamic  accent,",
        "         ghost"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Accents",
      "lines": [
        "An accent is LOUDER",
        "than your own",
        "strokes: their",
        "median + Accent +",
        "(15). A ghost: the",
        "median - Ghost -",
        "(20).",
        "",
        "Hit everything hard",
        "and nothing stands",
        "out.",
        "",
        "Scored apart: dyn",
        "30%. A soft accent",
        "is never a wrong",
        "note."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Clean at tempo",
      "lines": [
        "A drill is learned",
        "when you play it",
        "CLEAN at its written",
        "tempo:",
        "",
        "90% of notes right -",
        "the right drum (and",
        "hand, on Sticking",
        "strict), no strays -",
        "and the spread in",
        "the Strict window.",
        "",
        "Your % is the",
        "fastest clean take.",
        "100% earns the tick",
        "- not on Loose,",
        "Guide pads or Study."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The map",
      "lines": [
        "The Learning Path is",
        "a map: an island per",
        "stage. On an island,",
        "a building per part:",
        "a signpost for its",
        "lessons, a bell for",
        "Ear, a clock for",
        "Time, a workshop for",
        "Hands, a stage for",
        "Grooves, a cove for",
        "the electives, a",
        "fort for the",
        "checkpoint.",
        "",
        "PAD    walk there,",
        "       again: go in",
        "JOG    walk",
        "CLICK  go in",
        "PLAY   Continue",
        "BACK   up",
        "",
        "A flag: done. Ground",
        "rising: how much is",
        "learned. A dot:",
        "reviews due.",
        "",
        "SHIFT+CLICK: Show as",
        "list, for Review.",
        "",
        "The path moves:",
        "CLICK zooms into an",
        "island, BACK out. A",
        "place done raises",
        "its flag and walks",
        "you on; a stage done",
        "has fireworks and",
        "sails to the next.",
        "Any key or pad skips",
        "it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Learning Path",
      "lines": [
        "Seven stages, first",
        "beat to pro. In",
        "each: Lessons, Ear,",
        "Time, Hands,",
        "Grooves, Electives,",
        "and the Checkpoint",
        "last.",
        "",
        "Continue opens the",
        "next step. A step",
        "sets Speed to its",
        "target: 45/60 = best",
        "45%, the step asks",
        "60. Pass a stage's",
        "Checkpoint to move",
        "on.",
        "",
        "SHIFT+CLICK a stage:",
        "skip it, start the",
        "path there, or Test",
        "out: checkpoint.",
        "Settings > Start at:",
        "where it starts.",
        "Settings > Advanced",
        "> Learning Path:",
        "tracks, styles,",
        "rungs, intros."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Review",
      "lines": [
        "What you learned",
        "comes back after 1,",
        "3, 7, 14 and 30",
        "days. Continue",
        "offers one review,",
        "then one new step.",
        "",
        "A clean take at",
        "tempo moves it",
        "further out; a slip",
        "brings it back",
        "tomorrow. Slow",
        "practice never",
        "counts as a slip,",
        "and your best never",
        "drops."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Progress",
      "lines": [
        "Overall and each",
        "track: drills",
        "learned, as a line",
        "along real time.",
        "",
        "Then every drill you",
        "played: CLICK for",
        "its takes' chart,",
        "the 100% line",
        "dotted, clean takes",
        "filled.",
        "",
        "In a chart the JOG",
        "goes on to the next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The result",
      "lines": [
        "Big: the speed you",
        "played, % of",
        "written. Beside it:",
        "% right and the",
        "spread; the one that",
        "stopped it is",
        "inverted. Not clean:",
        "big is % right, and",
        "under it what cost",
        "the most. dyn 30%:",
        "how accents and",
        "ghosts sounded.",
        "",
        "JOG back: the take",
        "as you played it -",
        "rings hit, crosses",
        "missed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Ladder",
      "lines": [
        "SHIFT+CLICK a drill,",
        "Practise: Ladder.",
        "",
        "Starts at 70% of the",
        "drill's tempo and",
        "climbs through it.",
        "Play N bars clean",
        "and it goes up. Slip",
        "and the rung plays",
        "again; slip twice",
        "and it stops.",
        "",
        "Your score is the",
        "top clean tempo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Clock",
      "lines": [
        "SHIFT+CLICK a drill,",
        "Practise: Clock.",
        "",
        "The click plays for",
        "four bars, then",
        "stops and you keep",
        "time. Your drift",
        "shows live while it",
        "is silent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Quiz",
      "lines": [
        "Guess and Hear: drum",
        "- play the drum",
        "asked for.",
        "",
        "Pick: drum, Hear:",
        "subdivision and",
        "Pick: groove name",
        "what you heard.",
        "Pick: drum's answers",
        "are the kit's own",
        "pads, each drum lit",
        "in its colour. The",
        "others sit on the",
        "bottom row, one",
        "coloured pad each.",
        "Press it, or JOG and",
        "CLICK.",
        "",
        "REC is help; PLAY",
        "plays the question",
        "again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Settings",
      "lines": [
        "One short page:",
        "Pads      the layout",
        "Pad map   see it,",
        "          edit it",
        "Flip      for the",
        "          left hand",
        "Click     on or off",
        "Start at  the stage",
        "          the path",
        "          starts at",
        "Advanced  the rest",
        "",
        "Advanced:",
        "Learning Path",
        "          what",
        "          Continue",
        "          offers",
        "Practice  tempo,",
        "          reading,",
        "          judging",
        "Sound     click sub,",
        "          latency",
        "MIDI      where hits",
        "          go",
        "Help      tips and",
        "          welcome",
        "",
        "BACK walks up a",
        "page. SHIFT+CLICK",
        "in a drill opens",
        "Settings; again, or",
        "on any of its pages,",
        "closes it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Latency",
      "lines": [
        "If every hit reads",
        "late by the same",
        "amount, that is your",
        "rig, not you.",
        "",
        "Settings > Advanced",
        "> Sound > Latency",
        "takes it off",
        "every reading."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sound",
      "lines": [
        "The module has its",
        "own kit and click.",
        "Nothing to set up.",
        "",
        "Settings > Advanced",
        "> MIDI: MIDI out can",
        "send to",
        "a track or USB",
        "instead."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
